        <p class="profile-detail-region">City · Ancient Near East</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Persepolis</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 515 BCE – 330 BCE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">The earliest remains date to 515 BCE; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darius-i">Darius I</a> built the terrace and the palaces, and the French archaeologist André Godard believed that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrus-the-great">Cyrus the Great</a> had chosen the site.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On a terrace leaning on Rahmat Mountain, near the small river Pulvar, in the plains of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marvdasht">Marvdasht</a>, encircled by the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagros-mountains">Zagros Mountains</a>, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fars">Fars province</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apadana">Apadana</a> and its stairway reliefs; the Gate of All Nations; the Hundred-Columns Palace; the Tachara and Hadish palaces; the burning of the palaces in 330 BCE; the Persepolis Fortification Archive; the trilingual royal inscriptions that helped the decipherment of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuneiform">cuneiform</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Persepolis is a ruin and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fars">Fars province</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>.</span></div>
